course: dictionary
lesson: 443
title: Architect: the person who designs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An architect is a person whose job is to design buildings. Before anything is built, the architect draws plans that show what the building will look like and how it should be put together. «An architect designs a building and works with engineers; builders, electricians, plumbers and many others build it.» The clues are designs and build: the architect plans, and other people do the building.
explain: Read the rest of the sentence to see who does what. Engineers check that the building will stand up, and a big team of builders makes it real. The architect draws the plans first. Try your meaning in the sentence: "an architect draws the plans for a building" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The word has a second meaning. «The architect of the peace deal» means the person who planned it or made it happen. Here the word does not mean a building at all. The words around it, such as "peace deal", are the clues, so always check the context before you decide what a word means.
explain: Some words join together in phrases. A landscape architect designs gardens and parks, and a trained architect has studied for years to do the job. The word "of" shows what the architect made: the architect of something.
fact: An architect is a person who designs buildings and draws the plans for how they should be built.
fact: «The architect of the peace deal» means the person who planned it or made it happen.
fact: «Architecture» is the art of designing buildings.
fact: The Sydney Opera House was designed by the Danish architect Jørn Utzon and opened in 1973; its roofs are often compared to sails.
fact: Architects use shapes, measuring, scale drawings and angles, which is why maths is part of the job.
exercise: «An architect designs a building and works with engineers.» Who draws the plans for a building? | Electricians | *An architect | Builders | Plumbers
exercise: In «the architect of the peace deal», what does architect mean? | A person who paints pictures | A person who fixes pipes | *A person who planned it or made it happen | A person who builds houses
exercise: «Architecture is the art of designing buildings.» What is architecture? | The art of cooking food | The job of driving buses | *The art of designing buildings | The art of painting pictures
test: Who checks that a building will stand up? | Builders | Architects | *Engineers | Painters
test: In «designed by the Danish architect Jørn Utzon», which word tells you who made the design? | *architect | opened | Sydney | arts
exam: Read this: «An architect draws the plans, engineers check the building will stand up, and a big team of builders actually makes it.» Which person's job is to draw the plans? | Builder | Engineer | *Architect | Electrician
